{
    "schema":  1,
    "suite":  "states",
    "description":  "Save states through the console sessions, by REWINDING: each game is played for a fixed number of frames twice, once straight and once with a state taken after frame N and loaded back after frame M (frames N+1 to M are played again with the same pad; the sound of the first pass is dropped). A complete state ends the run on the very picture, sound and colours of the straight run, so both cases of a pair carry the SAME golden: if one field of the machine were left out of the state, the rewind case would differ from the plain one. Every case is a console session built the way the apps build it (UAT run-suite, kind session, Workshop --session-test --rewind). The SNES cases cover the plain boards, the DSP-1 (homemade), the SA-1 and the Super FX / Super FX 2; the others are one game each of the Game Boy, Master System, Game Gear and Genesis. The goldens say what this build did when they were recorded (nothing moved); the proof that a state is complete is that the two cases of a pair agree, and Workshop --snes-state-test (and --md-state-test, --smstest --only sessionstate) which compare every field. A ROM that is not on this machine SKIPs.",
